{# THE SETTINGS SECTION'S FRAME — the head every one of its screens wears.

   SETTINGS WEARS THE AREA IDIOM (ruled 2026-09-20), and the area tab header
   rule with it: the SAME head on every screen — the section's name — with a
   subline that changes per screen to say what THIS one answers. A reader who
   has learnt an area has learnt this.

   ONE CONTROL IN THE ACTION ROW, and it is a statement rather than a switch:
   everything in this section is true of the whole installation, and a scope
   dropdown here would have one setting for ever. An area's own settings are
   on the area and a module's are on that module's Configure page, which is
   what the chip is saying.

   THE STRIP IS THE SECTION'S SCREENS, from the one declaration the sidebar's
   subtree is built from — so a tab and a sidebar child cannot disagree about
   which screens the section has.

   A SCREEN FILLS `shell_page` AND NOTHING ELSE. It types no head, no strip
   and no crumb; those are the frame's, here as everywhere. #}
{% extends '@Shell/page.html.twig' %}

{% block title %}{{ title }}{% endblock %}

{% block shell_breadcrumbs %}
    {%- set brand = shell_brand() -%}
    <a href="{{ brand.url }}">{{ brand.name }}</a> / settings
{% endblock %}

{% block shell_page_title %}{{ title }}{% endblock %}
{% block shell_page_subtitle %}{{ subtitle }}{% endblock %}

{% block shell_page_actions %}<span class="chip acc">{{ scope }}</span>{% endblock %}

{% block shell_page_tabs %}
    {%- include '@Shell/_area_tabs.html.twig' with {tabs: tabs} only -%}
{% endblock %}
